extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market printed 85-87 (cache p086-p088, page_offset 1). The section opens in the right column of printed 85 after the Plant-People, the Pythonan R.C.C. block runs down printed 86 into the left column of 87, and the Pythonan Scholar/Philosopher or Artist R.C.C. ends on 87 before the Rulian Translator. Printed 86 and 87 read off 200 dpi renders on 2026-11-19; every figure below matches the render. The text layer sets P.E. as RE. and the scholar''s money as lD6x 1,000. || NAME: id pythonan; the block is headed Pythonan R.C.C., NPC Villain and Optional Player Character. || VARIANT: the Scholar/Philosopher or Artist R.C.C. is the scholar variant (ruling of 2026-11-18), with a plain pythonan variant beside it. A variant may add occ_skills and override starting_money, so its twelve R.C.C. skill lines and its 1D6x1,000 are stored; its Related and Secondary skill lists and its equipment cannot be stated by a variant (VARIANT_OVERRIDES), and that it is played without an O.C.C. has no key, so all three are a restriction line. || ATTRIBUTES: as printed. || POOLS: M.D.C. P.E. +1D6 per level; the S.D.C.-world figures are prose. P.P.E. 3D6+10, the usual for a magic O.C.C. if selected, so yields_to_occupation hands ppe_base to a magic occupation. Horror Factor 12. men_of_arms false: a race. || XP: the Average Level of Experience note says use the experience table of the dragon regardless of the chosen O.C.C. or R.C.C., so xp_table copies production''s dragon-hatchling ladder, read --remote 2026-11-19 (Nate''s decision 2026-09-26), and keeps_xp_table is true. || OCCUPATIONS: half the O.C.C. Related and Secondary skills is pairing_counts factor 0.5 on both, for every occupation. A Practitioner of Magic''s Secondary skills falling to none has no key short of naming every magic occupation id, and is a restriction line. || PSIONICS: Master Psychic, I.S.P. M.E. x3 +2D6 per level. The fourteen listed powers are granted by production''s psionic_powers names (Telekinetic Push, Lift and Punch are three rows). One Physical power at level 1 is powers_starting 1 from Physical; levels 3, 6, 9, 12 and 15 Physical and 5, 10 and 15 Super are the schedule. The magic-O.C.C. case (no additional powers, 1D6 I.S.P. per level) is prose and a schedule note. Advanced Telekinesis and the Telekinetic Body Field are class abilities with their I.S.P. costs in the text (ruling of 2026-11-18), not psionic_powers rows. The save threshold of 10 is prose. || COMBAT: four attacks regardless of O.C.C. is attacks_base 4 with ignores_style_attacks; +1 at levels 4, 8 and 12. No conventional hand to hand, so hand_to_hand costs {}. R.C.C. bonuses +2 initiative, +3 dodge, +3 pull punch, +3 roll, +2 vs possession and +4 vs Horror Factor are stored; the strike and parry bonuses by attack and the telekinetic weapon bonuses are conditional and prose. That O.C.C. bonuses do not apply has no key and is a restriction line. Natural attacks keep their printed S.D.C. damage as prose. || SKILLS: the race has no R.C.C. skill list; climb, swim, prowl and track by smell are natural abilities in prose. The race''s natural +10% to art related skills, to learn to read and to Seduction is folded into the scholar''s Art, Whittling & Sculpting, Literacy and Seduction, each note saying so. The three languages at 98% are choice groups from Language: Other with bonus 48, per_level 0. Basic Math and Anthropology store the scholar''s figure; the artist''s halved bonus is in the note. || EQUIPMENT: per O.C.C., minus body armor and clothing; the scholar''s basic gear names no item, so none is granted. || NOT STORED: size, weight, life span, habitat, value (200,000-600,000 credits), allies and enemies are in the body."
---

## Lore

Pythonans look like large snakes scaled in greens, golds and blacks, and are easily taken for animals or supernatural predators. They are in fact intelligent, civilized beings who respect all life, love philosophy and science, find magic and human behavior fascinating, and have a keen sense of humor and irony. They work tools with a prehensile tail and with telekinesis, building simple tools, shaping pottery, turning pages, operating machines and using weapons; many are amateur or professional artists.

Their homeworld is green, with small settlements and simple technology, but they are advanced thinkers in science, philosophy, communication, diplomacy, the arts and behavior. Most are scholars and philosophers, and about one in five practices magic (mainly Ley Line Walkers, Mystics, Shifters and Temporal Wizards). A few hundred free Pythonans have reached Rifts Earth, but most were brought as property for the Splugorth slave markets, where demons and humanoids find them exotic companions, teachers and artisans. They are cool-headed, slow to anger and introspective.

## Body

They are 7 to 9 feet (2.1 to 2.7 m) long and weigh 150 to 250 lbs (67.5 to 112.5 kg). Average life span is 200 years. NPC villains are level 1D4+4.

## GM Notes

Habitat: prefer warm climates but are found almost anywhere, using the same shelter and fire as humanoids to stay warm; free Pythonans are scattered about the globe and the Megaverse. Value: 200,000 to 600,000 credits is common, and some renowned artists command more; evil ones with the makings of spies, thieves or assassins can start bidding wars. Allies: most enjoy humans and D-Bees, though their appearance means they are often persecuted or never fully trusted; they are comfortable among dragons and creatures of magic, and uneasy among demons unless evil. Enemies: evil reptilian beings, above all the Lyvorkkians, who can briefly control the minds of other intelligent reptiles; they know the Splugorth and demons for the evil enslavers they are.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'pythonan');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'pythonan';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-pythonan-class.sql');
